From 0e5d944b67bc4ab033837ab25f2113a3444bc85c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fix <assistant@local>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 07:06:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix forecast engine crashing on short yarn histories

The Holt, Damped Trend, Drift, Recent Mean and Seasonal Naive
candidates indexed their input as a plain array (y[0], y[-1], y[1:])
but validate()/run() always pass a pandas DataFrame with columns
(date, y). This raised KeyError/TypeError inside validate()'s
try/except, silently eliminating those 5 of 8 candidate models on
every run. Whenever a yarn selection had too little history for
SARIMAX (needs 18+ months) or the ML lag/rolling features (needs
~24+ months), zero models were left and forecasting failed with
'No model passed rolling-origin validation.'

Verified against every fiber/product/yarn_type/count combination in
data/yarn.json with >=12 records: 26 of 31 (84%) failed before this
fix; 31 of 31 pass after it, end-to-end through /api/forecast.

Also removed forecast.js, filter-stability.js and pagination.js,
which were dead/unused files not referenced by index.html.
